<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The Progression pack's preset for Loot Scavenging (spec, "The Progression pack").

     NOT ACTIVE BY DEFAULT. This folder is outside Defs/ and Patches/, so the game never loads it. The pack's author copies
     this file into the pack's own Patches/ folder (it needs nothing else; it patches only Loot Scavenging's defaults def).

     What it does: the Progression defaults stay as they are (out-of-reach gear becomes scrap from every non-colony group,
     on death, downed and strip, with prisoners on), and instant disassembly returns era-typical yields. The item-based
     yield would hand a tribal colony plasteel on the battlefield with no bench, so the yield is also locked: the page
     shows it disabled with a reason and nothing else can switch it.

     Not yet verified against the pack: the pack's own benches and materials per era, and where Progression: Core stores
     the colony's era (spec, "Open questions"). The spec table is drawn from the Workshop descriptions only. Until those
     are checked, this file patches no tier table entries; when they are, add the pack's benches and materials here as
     patches on LS_ScrapTier_* (see Defs/ScrapTiers.xml for the form). -->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/LootScavenging.SettingsDefaultsDef[defName="LS_SettingsDefaults"]/values/rules/disassemblyYield</xpath>
    <value>
      <disassemblyYield>EraTypical</disassemblyYield>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/LootScavenging.SettingsDefaultsDef[defName="LS_SettingsDefaults"]/locked</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>rules.disassemblyYield</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
